state.case_summary:
A child weighing 30 kg, without any comorbidities and allergies, not taking any long-term medications, presented with erythematous, infiltrating, well-demarcated skin lesions located on the face, chest, abdomen, and limbs. The patient reported frequent contact with stray cats.

Erythematous, infiltrating, well-demarcated skin lesions were observed on the face, chest, abdomen, and limbs.

